# Cloudflare Pages reads this file to attach extra response headers by path
# pattern. See README.md — this site deploys to Cloudflare Pages on every
# `git push`.
#
# activities.json is intentionally NOT covered here: it's rewritten by every
# sync.py run and must keep revalidating on each visit, or a sync wouldn't
# show up for a returning visitor until the browser's cache expired on its
# own.
#
# Stream files are close to immutable (each is fetched once per activity id
# and normally never touched again) but not quite: sync.py's `--backfill-hr`
# phase can rewrite an existing id's stream file in place, once, if that
# activity later gets heart-rate data Strava didn't have at initial fetch
# time (see fetch_stream/backfill_hr in sync.py). A plain long max-age
# (not `immutable`) still cuts a real cost — selecting an activity a second
# time within the cache window skips the network round-trip for its stream
# entirely — while bounding staleness to at most a week if a backfill run
# ever touches an id a visitor already has cached.
/data/streams/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
